            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery dissection and acute infarction due to blunt trauma: report of a case.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>971-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Coronary artery dissection occurring after a nonpenetrating chest trauma is extremely rare. We describe herein the case of a 43-year-old man who suffered traumatic myocardial infarction after an intimal tear of the right coronary artery had been inflicted by a horse stepping on his back.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
